Local changes (the only ones; every other file is as upstream):

  src/rtkpos.c, rtkpos() (line 2381 upstream, "} else rtk->sol.time=obs[0].time;"): the branch that
  skips the single point positioning of an epoch (when the variance of the position is below
  STD_PREC_VAR_THRESH) now also copies the time mark of the epoch,
      } else { rtk->sol.time=obs[0].time; rtk->sol.eventime=obs[0].eventime; }
  pntpos() (pntpos.c, sol->eventime = obs[0].eventime) is the only place that sets it, so upstream an
  event (RINEX epoch flag 5, u-blox TIM-TM2) on such an epoch was lost and the mark of an earlier epoch
  was written again on later ones: on the 30 s samples of tests/data/rtklib (3040 against 0759) two
  of four marks were missing from <solution>_events.pos in forward, backward and combined mode. With
  the change all four are written, and the .pos files are byte for byte the same. To be reported upstream.

Only the sources rnx2rtkp is built from (app/consapp/rnx2rtkp/gcc/makefile) are kept, unchanged
(but for the change above), in src/:
rtklib.h and rtkcmn trace rinex rtkpos postpos solution lambda geoid sbas preceph pntpos
ephemeris options ppp ppp_ar rtcm rtcm2 rtcm3 rtcm3e ionex tides (.c), and, from 0.8 of the core,
those of convbin's conversion of raw receiver logs (app/consapp/convbin/gcc/makefile) with two of its
receiver decoders, unchanged too: src/convrnx.c, src/rcvraw.c, src/rcv/ublox.c and src/rcv/novatel.c.
Streams, servers, downloads and the applications are left out. Compile-time settings come from
native/build.rs; the callbacks RTKLIB asks of an application are in native/src/ppk_shim.c.

The receiver decoders (src/rcv) were vendored one by one after reading the header of each. No file
of src/rcv names a licence: each has a copyright line, most with "All rights reserved". BSD 2-clause
for ublox.c and novatel.c is an inference, not a statement in the files: their copyright holder,
T. Takasu, is the one of license.txt, the BSD 2-clause licence (compatible with the GPL-2.0-or-later
of the core) under which RTKLIB distributes its sources. Only those two are here.

  ublox.c     "Copyright (C) 2007-2020 by T.TAKASU" and "Copyright (C) 2014 by T.SUZUKI": RTKLIB's
              author, the copyright holder of license.txt (T. Suzuki's changes are part of RTKLIB's
              own releases), "All rights reserved", no licence named. Vendored: u-blox UBX (RXM-RAWX,
              RXM-SFRBX, TIM-TM2, ...).
  novatel.c   "Copyright (C) 2007-2020 by T.TAKASU, All rights reserved", no licence named. Vendored:
              NovAtel OEM4/OEMV/OEM6/OEM7, OEMStar.
  septentrio.c "Copyright (C) 2013 by Fabrizio Tappero. Copyright (C) 2015 by Jens Reimann": other
              authors, no licence in the file. Not vendored.
  rt17.c      "Copyright (C) 2016 Daniel A. Cook, All rights reserved. Copyright (C) 2020 T.TAKASU",
              and "Copyright (C) 2014, 2016 by Daniel A. Cook. All Rights Reserved." in its text, "written
              ... for inclusion into the RTKLIB library", with no licence named. Not vendored.
  unicore.c   "Copyright (C) 2024 Avinab Malla, All rights reserved.", no licence in the file. Not
              vendored.
  crescent.c, skytraq.c, javad.c, nvs.c, binex.c, swiftnav.c, tersus.c, comnav.c: formats the
              program does not take; not looked at, not vendored.

These files are distributed inside RTKLIB under its BSD 2-clause licence, and they may well be
covered by it; but the headers of septentrio.c, rt17.c and unicore.c name authors other than the
holder of license.txt and reserve their rights without naming a licence, so they stay out until
their authors (or RTKLIB's maintainers) state it. The entry points that rcvraw.c calls for them, and
for the other receivers, are stubs of ours in native/src/rcv_stubs.c, which decode nothing;
ppg_convbin() refuses those formats by name (code -6). RTCM 3 needs no file of src/rcv: rtcm.c and
rtcm3.c decode it.

RINEX is never an input of convrnx() here (ppg_convbin() takes u-blox, RTCM 3 and NovAtel only):
convrnx() would decompress a compressed RINEX file through a shell command (rtk_uncompress).

Also left out: src/sofa.c, which the makefile of rnx2rtkp lists. It is a bundle of routines of the
IAU SOFA library (epv00 and moon98 with the functions they need), and SOFA has a licence of its
own, not BSD: its notes, which the file refers to, are in lib/sofa/src of the upstream repository
and are not part of this package. rtkcmn.c calls the two functions only if SUNPOS_SOFA or
MOONPOS_SOFA is defined, an option for more accurate positions of the Sun and the Moon. Neither
is defined here (nor in the makefile of rnx2rtkp): sunpos_eci() and moonpos_eci() take RTKLIB's
own series (their #else branches), and nothing refers to sofa.c (rtkcmn.c only declares the two
functions). sunmoonpos() is reached from the tide corrections (tides.c), PPP (ppp.c) and the
satellite antenna offsets of precise ephemerides (preceph.c), none of which the post-processing
of this package uses. RTKLIB's sample data (a static and a kinematic run) gives the same solution
files, byte for byte, with and without it. Do not put it back, or define either macro, without
carrying the SOFA licence in this package.
